{"ref":"BDB, עָגַב","hw":"עָגַב","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">עָגַב</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. have inordinate affection, lust (</strong>cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">عَجِبَ</span> <em>wonder, admire</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">عَجِيبٌ</span> <em>beloved;</em> and (on sens. obsc. in NH) Levy<sup>NHWB iii. 616</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  Pf. 3 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">עָֽגְבָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.7\">Ez 23:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.12\">12</a>; Impf. 3 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַתַּעְגַּב</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.5\">5</a>, + v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:16\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.16\">16</a> Kt (Qr <span dir=\"rtl\">וַתַּעְגְּבָה</span>), <span dir=\"rtl\">וַתַּעְגְּבַה</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.20\">20</a> (Ew<sup>§ 191 c</sup> Ol<sup>§ 228 b</sup>); Pt. pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֹגְבִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:30\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.30\">Je 4:30</a>;—<em>lust</em> after <span dir=\"rtl\">(עַל־)</span>, only in fig. of relations of Samaria and Jerus. (personif.) with foreigners <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.5\">Ez 23:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:16\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.16\">16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.20\">20</a>, so c. acc. v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.7\">7</a>; pt. as subst. <em>paramours</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:30\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.30\">Je 4:30</a>.","next":"BDB, עָגָב","prev":"BDB, עֹג"}